cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use twosystems, please cite it as below."
title: "twosystems: a calibrated watchman for AI coding agents"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Shashikant
    alias: shashikantdev3
repository-code: "https://github.com/shashikantdev3/twosystems"
url: "https://github.com/shashikantdev3/twosystems"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  twosystems, in development, will watch AI coding agent sessions (Claude
  Code, GitHub Copilot in VS Code, Cursor, Windsurf), notice when the agent
  is stuck or when the work has moved on, suggest a better next step, and
  report token savings verified with a randomized holdout. A small decision
  model (System 1) makes calibrated calls; a larger model (System 2, off by
  default) and the user handle the uncertain cases.
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - claude-code
  - github-copilot
  - token-optimization
  - decision-models
  - calibration
  - llm-cost
